        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f5d7a562-b041-55b7-8187-4d88424b3570",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Garth Richardson, Jack Richardson, Pete Ham, Ron Griffiths, David \"Dai\" Jenkins\n- Bands: Badfinger, The Iveys, Daughters of Mara\n- Companies: Virgin Records\n- Places: Swansea, Wales\n- Topics: music production, album releases\n\nFacts:\n- In 1961, Pete Ham, Ron Griffiths, and David \"Dai\" Jenkins formed The Iveys in Swansea, Wales.\n- Badfinger evolved from the earlier group The Iveys.\n- Jack Richardson was a Canadian music producer whose credits included Alice Cooper, The Guess Who, Badfinger, and Poco.\n- Garth Richardson is the son of Canadian music producer Jack Richardson.\n- Daughters of Mara released its first album, I Am Destroyer, on Virgin Records.\n- Garth Richardson produced Daughters of Mara's first album, I Am Destroyer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
